# Connect your own domain

{% info title="SMTP-DOCS-TODO: Screenshot pending (blog-custom-domain)" %}
**SMTP-DOCS-TODO screenshot:blog-custom-domain.** Capture the Console screen that shows the MX and TXT records for a new email domain. Dark theme, 1460x822 viewport at 2x, screenshot mode on. Save as `/images/blog/announcing-function-email-triggers/custom-domain.avif`, then replace this block with the image.
{% /info %}

You can connect a domain that you own, such as `mail.example.com`. Email to any address at that domain executes your function, so use a domain or subdomain that receives no other email. Turn on the email trigger first, then add the domain and two DNS records at your DNS provider:

- An `MX` record that sends the email of the domain to the Appwrite mail server that the Console shows.
- A `TXT` record at `_appwrite.mail.example.com` with your project ID, which proves that you own the domain.

The email rule and the HTTP rule of a domain are separate, so one domain can have both. DNS does not allow an `MX` record on a name that has a `CNAME` record, so if your site uses a `CNAME` record on `support.example.com`, receive email on another subdomain, such as `mail.example.com`.

